From cf7ce44820ba0897c7e8d7399fe8071b8fd3931e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: friedger <mail@friedger.de>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:56:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] feat(oidc): logout through the provider, branded
 sign-in errors, app revoke

Belfry's apps sign in silently, so logging out of an app or of the
dashboard has to end the provider session as well, or the next tab signs
the participant straight back in.

- GET /api/auth/oidc/logout?return_to=<url> clears keycast_session and
  redirects to the provider's end_session_endpoint. The provider's
  invalidation flow ends at GET /api/auth/oidc/logged-out, which returns
  to return_to (a same-origin path, or an origin of one of the tenant's
  registered clients; anything else goes to /). The dashboard's sign-out
  uses it.
- POST /api/oauth/revoke (RFC 7009, public CORS): an app revokes its own
  authorization with the refresh token from the token response.
- Trusted clients: each token exchange revokes the user's authorizations
  for that client that never connected within 10 minutes and the
  connected ones beyond the five most recently active, so silent
  sign-ins on new browsers no longer pile up on the apps page.
- One flow cookie per sign-in (keycast_oidc_<state prefix>), so a silent
  try in a second tab no longer turns a pending magic-link sign-in into
  "State mismatch". The single legacy cookie is still read.
- Sign-in error pages in the Open Source Village look, with plain
  messages and a button that starts the sign-in again.
